   "html_text": "A fair coin is tossed. If it comes up heads, you receive $2. If it comes up tails, the coin is tossed for a second time. If it then comes up heads, you receive $4. If it comes up tails, the coin is tossed for a third time. If it then comes up heads, you receive $8. If it comes up tails, the coin is tossed for a fourth time. And so on. We continue until the coin comes up heads. If this takes n tosses, then you win $ ⟦M⟧ .",
   "md_text": "A fair coin is tossed. If it comes up heads, you receive ⟦M⟧ 4. If it comes up tails, the coin is tossed for a third time. If it then comes up heads, you receive ⟦M⟧ ⟦M⟧ ."
  },
  {
   "kind": "replace",
   "i": 309,
   "j": 315,
   "ratio": 0.858252427184466,
   "shape_h": "p",
   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "How much should you be prepared to pay to play this game? You have a 1/2 chance of winning $2; and a 1/4 chance of winning $4; and a 1/8 chance of winning $8; ….; and a ⟦M⟧ chance of winning $ ⟦M⟧ ; and … . Hence, your expected payoff from playing the St. Petersburg game is infinite:",
   "md_text": "How much should you be prepared to pay to play this game? You have a 1/2 chance of winning ⟦M⟧ 4; and a 1/8 chance of winning ⟦M⟧ 1/2^n ⟦M⟧ ⟦M⟧ ; and … . Hence, your expected payoff from playing the St. Petersburg game is infinite:"
  }
