   "html_text": "In 1915 Einstein introduced general relativity, and our conception of the universe is based on it. General relativity rests on a conception of space and time—or better, space-time matter—that stands in opposition to the Newtonian one we have described above. In Einstein’s theory, space-time is deformable and its shape depends on the presence of matter. Space-time is, in technical terms, a four-dimensional manifold. We may think of an ⟦M⟧ -dimensional manifold as a set of ⟦M⟧ -tuples of real numb",
